  "finding": "Edition163 measures complete recorded-object workflows over three existing recordings and four accepted world revisions. Exact, process-local recording reuse reduced measured task cost across the two comparison pairs; source, numerical native trace and actual report evidence match exactly. Mean paired change: 61.9% less task time. This is a small exposed local study, not a general speed guarantee.",
  "validation": "71 selected Java checks and 177 desktop checks passed without failures or skips. Three halfway-time labels and exact poses passed actual Chromium checks. Four final Java/Electron sessions completed sixteen durable chat workflows, four accepted revisions per session, retained skills, forced original reconstruction, abrupt restart, source-corruption refusal and cold verification. One camera episode and two generated recordings remain three distinct source sequences; repetition does not add physical evidence. New physical validation remains pending."
